```

The exact Pi 0.84.0 regular-pane run independently rendered `Error: music session endpoint is occupied by an unclassifiable peer` while inspection found Node PID 13328 running the resolved daemon entry and holding `/tmp/naxodev-music-501/s.sock` (UID 501, mode 0600). A direct client then completed a healthy hello against that endpoint.

The original OpenCode regular-pane run used the supplied checkout directory and rendered `1 plugin failed`; `/plugins` showed the bounded host diagnostic `ENOENT .../packages/opencode-music-player/tui`.

### Green after the fix

- Exact Pi 0.84.0, `--no-extensions -e <absolute checkout package>`, `PI_OFFLINE=1`, and an ownership-checked temporary profile initialized `music-dock` without the endpoint error. Host PID 15236 was Node; normal exit followed by the idle grace removed daemon, socket, marker, and bind lock.
- Exact OpenCode `opencode2 v0.0.0-next-17386` loaded absolute checkout `packages/opencode-music-player/index.tsx` from an ownership-checked isolated config. It rendered `▶︎ Wrecked - Kiasmos`, without `1 plugin failed`; inspection saw one Node daemon holding the 0600 socket. Normal exit plus idle grace removed all runtime artifacts.
- Each temporary root was a current-UID, non-symlink direct child of its temporary base and was removed by its launch-shell trap. No playback transport command was sent.

