## Residual risks

The retry is deliberately limited to a reset observed while this exact workflow owns the marker and has launched the daemon. A reset/malformed peer observed without that ownership remains terminal `occupied` and is never unlinked. This phase covers independent initialization only; it does not claim mixed-host controls, Pi reload survival, or Pi-exit isolation.
